<h2 style="margin:0 0 14px 0;font-size:22px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;"><%= @brand.name %> now works with Claude</h2>

<p>Hi <%= @user.first_name.presence || 'there' %>,</p>

<p>
  AI Apps is now turned on for <strong><%= @company.name %></strong>. Your team can add <%= @brand.name %> to
  Claude and ask it about leads, deals, inventory, service, the books, budgets, install projects and commission
  plans, using the same information they already see in <%= @brand.name %>.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Step 1. Choose who can use it (admins)</h3>
<p>
  You are an admin, so you already have access. For anyone else, open
  <a style="color:<%= @brand_accent %>;" href="<%= @roles_url %>">Settings, Users, Roles &amp; Permissions</a> in <%= @brand.name %> and give their role
  the <strong>AI Connector</strong> permission: <strong>Read</strong> to connect, <strong>Update</strong> to let
  Claude make changes for them.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Step 2. Add the <%= @brand.name %> plugin in Claude</h3>
<p>The plugin brings both pieces at once: the connection to <%= @brand.name %> and six ready-made skills. You need a
  Claude Pro, Max, Team or Enterprise plan.</p>
<ol>
  <li>Open Claude at <a style="color:<%= @brand_accent %>;" href="https://claude.ai">claude.ai</a> or in the Claude desktop app.</li>
  <li>Select <strong>Customize</strong> (in the sidebar), then <strong>Plugins</strong>.</li>
  <li>Select <strong>Discover</strong>, search for <strong><%= @brand.name %></strong>, open it and select
      <strong>Add</strong>. Or use the button below to go straight to it.</li>
</ol>
<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0;">
  <a href="<%= @directory_url %>"
     style="display:inline-block;background:<%= @brand_accent %>;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;
            font-weight:bold;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:6px;">Add <%= @brand.name %> in Claude</a>
</p>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Step 3. Connect your <%= @brand.name %> account</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Still on the plugin's page, open its <strong>Connectors</strong> tab.</li>
  <li>Next to <strong><%= @brand.name %></strong>, select <strong>Add</strong> if it says Not added, then
      <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
  <li>Sign in with your <%= @brand.name %> email and password. To let Claude make changes (add notes, tasks,
      drafts), tick <strong>Also let it make changes</strong> on that screen, then approve.</li>
  <li>The connector now shows <strong>Connected</strong>. It also appears under <strong>Customize</strong>,
      <strong>Connectors</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p><em>On a Claude Team or Enterprise plan</em>, your Claude organization Owner may need to add the
  <%= @brand.name %> connector for the team first (they select <strong>Connect for your team</strong>). Each person
  then connects with their own <%= @brand.name %> login.</p>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Step 4. Use it in a chat</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Start a new chat. Select <strong>+</strong> in the message box, then <strong>Connectors</strong>, and make
      sure <strong><%= @brand.name %></strong> is switched on.</li>
  <li>Ask in plain words. The first time Claude uses a <%= @brand.name %> tool it may ask permission; choose
      <strong>Allow once</strong> or <strong>Always allow</strong>.</li>
  <li>To pick a skill yourself, type <strong>/</strong> in the message box and choose one of the
      <%= @brand.name %> skills.</li>
</ol>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Everyday questions</h3>
<ul>
  <li>"Show my open deals by stage."</li>
  <li>"Find Maria Lopez and tell me where her deal stands."</li>
  <li>"What three bedroom homes do we have in stock under $90,000?"</li>
  <li>"What tasks are due for me this week?"</li>
  <li>"Which service tickets are still open?"</li>
  <li>"Add a note to the Garcia lead: called, wants a tour Saturday."</li>
  <li>"Create a task for me to call John Lopez tomorrow at 10."</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Bigger jobs (these use the built in skills)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>"Which of my leads are going cold, and what should we do about them?"</li>
  <li>"My bank feed is behind. Help me get it caught up."</li>
  <li>"How are my install projects going this week? Draft the customer updates."</li>
  <li>"I want to rethink how my salespeople get paid. Walk me through it."</li>
  <li>"Help me rough out a budget for next year."</li>
  <li>"Help me close last month."</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="margin:22px 0 6px 0;font-size:16px;color:<%= @brand_primary %>;">Good to know</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Claude sees only what each person can see in <%= @brand.name %>, at their locations.</li>
  <li>It asks before every change, and every change is recorded. You can review and undo them under
      <a style="color:<%= @brand_accent %>;" href="<%= @ai_apps_url %>">Settings, Integrations, AI Apps</a>.</li>
  <li>It never messages your customers, activates campaigns, workflows, budgets or commission plans, pays bills
      or deletes records. Those stay in <%= @brand.name %>.</li>
  <li>Dealer cost and gross stay hidden from Claude unless you turn on "Let AI apps see dealer cost and gross"
      on the same AI Apps page.</li>
</ul>

<p>
  More detail: <a style="color:<%= @brand_accent %>;" href="<%= @docs_url %>"><%= @docs_url %></a>. Questions? Write to
  <a style="color:<%= @brand_accent %>;" href="mailto:<%= @brand.support_email %>"><%= @brand.support_email %></a>.
</p>
